## examples/core/core_window_web.pengu
## raylib [core] example - window web
##
## Example complexity rating: [★☆☆☆] 1/4
##
## Example originally created with raylib 1.3, last time updated with raylib 5.5
##
## This example has been adapted to compile for PLATFORM_WEB and PLATFORM_DESKTOP
## As you will notice, code structure is slightly different to the other examples
##
## Example licensed under an unmodified zlib/libpng license, which is an OSI-certified,
## BSD-like license that allows static linking with closed source software
##
## Copyright (c) 2015-2025 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5)
##
## ## PenguScript Port
## 1:1 translation of `examples/core/core_window_web.c` on top of the `raylibx`
## wrapper layer and `std.web`. The per-frame callback `update_draw_frame` is
## registered via `web.set_main_loop` under `when wasm:` and driven by a
## standard `SetTargetFPS` + `WindowShouldClose` loop on desktop targets.
##
## ## Example
## ```bash
## pengu run examples/core/core_window_web.pengu
## ```

# --- Imports ------------------------------------------------------------
import raylib
import raylibx.drawing as drawing
import raylibx.text as txt
import std.web

# --- Constants ----------------------------------------------------------
## Window width, in pixels.
const SCREEN_WIDTH as int is 800

## Window height, in pixels.
const SCREEN_HEIGHT as int is 450

## Target frames per second for desktop targets.
const TARGET_FPS as int is 60

# --- Helpers ------------------------------------------------------------
## Updates and draws a single frame.
##
## ## Notes
## Passed as a callback to `web.set_main_loop` on WebAssembly builds, and
## invoked directly inside the `WindowShouldClose` loop on desktop builds.
##
## ## Memory
## No allocation and nothing to release.
weave update_draw_frame into void:
    # Update
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Update variables here when extending this template
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------

    # Draw
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    calling drawing.begin_drawing
    calling drawing.clear_background with raylib.RAYWHITE

    calling txt.draw_text with "Welcome to raylib web structure!", 220, 200, 20, raylib.SKYBLUE

    calling drawing.end_drawing
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Entry point --------------------------------------------------------
## Opens the window and runs the main loop using `std.web` on WebAssembly or
## the standard desktop loop otherwise.
##
## ## Returns
## Process exit code: `0` when the window closes normally.
weave main into int:
    # Initialization
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    calling raylib.InitWindow with SCREEN_WIDTH, SCREEN_HEIGHT, "raylib [core] example - window web"
    defer calling raylib.CloseWindow

    when wasm:
        calling web.set_main_loop with update_draw_frame, 0, true
    else:
        calling raylib.SetTargetFPS with TARGET_FPS
        # -----------------------------------------------------------------

        # Main game loop
        while not calling raylib.WindowShouldClose:
            calling update_draw_frame

    return 0
